From 8e194d8089ff0b9cb019809fb3e95cb7382eae00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:00:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] apps: Adds wlmmixer, a volume mixer DockApp for
 PulseAudio and PipeWire.

Shows the volume of the default audio output (sink) in percent and as a
meter of increasing bars, and whether it is muted; similar to Window
Maker's `wmix`. The mouse wheel changes the volume in steps of 5% (up to
100%), a left click toggles mute, and a right or middle click runs
`pavucontrol`.

Talks to the sound server through the PulseAudio client library, which
works with PulseAudio and with PipeWire (through `pipewire-pulse`). It
subscribes to changes of sinks and of the server's default sink, so
changes made elsewhere (eg. `pactl`, keyboard volume keys) show up right
away, without polling. The PulseAudio mainloop runs in its own thread,
and wakes up the Wayland mainloop through an eventfd.

Without a sound server or without a default sink, the app shows "--".
It does not auto-spawn a server; if the server is missing or goes away,
it reconnects with an increasing delay (0.5 s up to 8 s).

Options: --mixer_command (default: pavucontrol, empty disables it),
--step (percent per wheel step), --max_volume (limit when raising with
the wheel, in percent).

libpulse is an optional dependency: Without it, wlmmixer is not built.
Volume computations are in wlm_volume, with unit tests in `apps_test`.
Adds a .desktop file and an icon.

Signed-off-by: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
